;; PM Nylon Guitar / plucked nylon-string guitar identified from recorded plucks.
;; Generated by tools/pm-guitar/build.py; edit engine.lisp.in, then regenerate.
;; Reference coefficients only: no PCM, recorded phase or spectral frames.
;;
;; One voice is one string: 32 stiff-string partials (complex modal
;; rotations). A pluck sets each partial's displacement from the measured
;; pluck of the nearest recorded pitch:
;;   a_k = L sin(pi k beta) k^-alpha exp(-(f_k/fc)^2) exp(body h(f_k) + detail d_k)
;; beta (pluck position), alpha (finger contact tilt), fc (fingertip/nail
;; roll-off), L and d_k belong to a recorded take; h(f) is the measured
;; body/radiation EQ shared by every note. Loss: sigma = s0 + b f^2, saturating.
;; The string drives a small bank of measured body resonances (air ~100 Hz,
;; top ~200 Hz ...), and the finger's contact adds a short noise burst.

